&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be building and scaling LLM-based systems that process billions of highly unstructured data points every day, extract precise information, and surface insights that insurers rely on for high-stakes decisions, along with the services, data models, and external-facing APIs that sit at the center of Kalepa. This is a problem the industry hasn&#39;t solved effectively yet, and you&#39;ll be working on cutting-edge challenges that require creativity and ambition. We&#39;re a small team where individual contributions have an outsized impact on both our technology and our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary range&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We differentiate our North America salary ranges using two geographical zones:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zone 1&lt;/strong&gt; (New York and San Francisco) - $246,000 to $314,000*&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zone 2&lt;/strong&gt; (all other locations in the US and Canada) - $222,000 to $314,000*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are primarily a remote company with employees across the US, Canada, and Europe. Our HQ is in New York city.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team is a mix of software engineers owning Kalepa’s IT integration platform (public APIs, control plane) and forward-deployed engineers who embed with clients to integrate atop Kalepa’s APIs. The team is tasked with ensuring Kalepa’s deployments are complete, high-quality, and conducive to self-service. The team will define clear criteria for deployment quality and build processes that raise that quality standard for every client. Where the codebase today limits extensibility, they plan and refactor for sustainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership areas&lt;/strong&gt;: Kalepa’s Public APIs and external docs; auth/SSO/permissions; control plane &amp;amp; admin tooling for configuring clients; adapters into external systems that build against Kalepa’s Public API.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical and project aspects of key backend initiatives: services, data models, asynchronous pipelines, and evals in Python on AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction for how Kalepa builds and operates LLM-based systems at scale: reliability, cost, latency, evaluation, and explainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead architectural discussions and decisions across the product; be a strong systems designer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver major product innovations in each release; take leadership in scoping new features and efforts for enhancement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage technical debt, deciding when to accrue it and when to pay it off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business and product owners to drive firm-wide decisions, pragmatically weighing data, resources, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the adoption of best practices for development, testing, and deployment; lead code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify product and testing improvement opportunities that cross services, modules, and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an ambassador for Kalepa internally and externally, including in recruiting and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling deliberately to multiply your own impact and that of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering experience building and operating backend systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have delivered as the tech lead on at least one major initiative or project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with LLMs in production and understand what it takes to deploy them at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know Python (our main stack), though we&#39;re open to strong candidates from other OO backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS and serverless technologies (Lambda, Step Functions), asynchronous workflows, and cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of relational databases and their performance tuning, ideally PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently a go-to resource for other engineering, product, or business staff in technical matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take full ownership of your work and drive projects to completion with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate proactively and persuasively with engineers, product, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive on experimentation and are excited by problems others are struggling with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with document pipelines and processing large amounts of data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building external-facing APIs or designing integrations with third-party systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in insurance, fintech, or another data-heavy regulated domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (based on experience level)*.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant equity options package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of PTO a year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global team offsites (2024 - Lisbon, 2025 - Cartagena, 2026 - Tbilisi).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy living/gym stipend.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile phone bill stipend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuing education credits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US employees only:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% covered medical, 100% covered vision and dental for individuals and families.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with employer contribution (regardless of employee contribution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*The salary range listed is an estimate and will vary based on a variety of factors. Final compensation will be determined during the offer stage based on relevant experience, performance during the interview process, and geographic location, and may therefore differ from the posted range.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

