&lt;li&gt;Exceptional, demonstrated, ability to close and grow large enterprise SaaS contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to quickly develop master-level knowledge of the industry and become a thought partners to your clients, prospects, and Kalepa’s leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience at an early-stage startup during hypergrowth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can independently develop and execute sales plans to exceed Kalepa’s targets, including prospecting at the senior executive level at enterprise organizations, including publicly traded companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills; ability to engage effectively with senior executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love to hustle: finding ways to get things done, destroying obstacles, and never taking no for an answer. The words “it can’t be done” don’t exist in your vocabulary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate, deeply motivated, and have a strong will to win. You are excited about bringing a world-class solution to clients and to helping them win in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be expected to spend several days per week meeting with clients and prospects in-person within your geography (Tri-state area or Midwest if based in Chicago)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent listener. You are perceptive to clients’ strategic priorities and business considerations. You serve as a trusted thought partner and always look for ways to enable clients further with our solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value open, frank, and respectful communication.&lt;/li&gt;
